      {
        "id": 137530,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-18T16:02:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We have official rulings that:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>If a target dealing damage is incapacitated it stops doing what it was doing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Once selected, the lowest/highest HP target doesn't reselect during that action.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I think that makes it pretty clear that the damage stops once Set is incapped.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Just to make the last logical step explicit:</p>\n<p>2a: Point 2 suggests that once the <em>source</em> of an action is selected, it also would not reselect during that action.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This has not been officially ruled to be the case yet, but I agree that it seems most consistent with prior rulings.</p>",
